d_at":"2026-10-18T09:39:27Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123663","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123663","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123663.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123663.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nSome objects (particularly query parameters/results) are meant to be reused by updating their members or just by passing the same instance into a function again. This idiom is usually taught by examples and tutorials, but it may not be obvious if you're just trying to use the API blindly. This PR adds an editor-only warning against the most common misuse case of allocating an object every physics tick.\r\n\r\n- Relevant for https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113970/\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n~~The template/include hell issue can probably be solved better; suggestions welcome.~~\r\n\r\n~~Perhaps the warning should be configurable and ignorable. It seems to me that if we put the threshold high enough (like the 60 ticks I'm proposing) then the user is probably definitely doing something wrong, so I didn't make it configurable. Let me know if I'm missing some common use case here.~~ It can be turned off now.\r\n\r\nAs an alternative, I first considered trying to use the GDScript analyzer to see where the instance is created (I wanted to check if it is assigned to a class member), but this is complicated since it would also be valid to put it in a container (like an array or a dictionary), and good luck detecting that case. Also, assigning to a class member is not yet a guarantee that this assignment isn't being done repeatedly (e.g. inside a function that gets called every frame or every physics tick).","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123663/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123663/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}